{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534005-new-to-st-ing-werewolf-the-dark-ages","id":1534005,"title":"New to ST'ing Werewolf the Dark Ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-10T17:12:45-07:00","id":1534005,"title":"New to ST'ing Werewolf the Dark Ages","content":"I'm new to ST'ing Werewolf and need some pointers. I have been running Vampire games since the mid/late 1990's and the mood is way different. Or am I wrong? Thnaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T19:20:09-07:00","id":1534006,"title":"","content":"No, you're quite right about that. That's part of the backlash against W5, in fact!<br /> <br /> In general, Vampire indulges in pessimistic and self-indulgent nihilism. There's no getting your humanity back, you're on a downward spiral that can only be halted at a low point, so do whatever! Every one is cursed! Nothing is good!<br /> <br /> Werewolf is the opposite. It's about digging in and keeping what's important around another day through the power of blood, sweat, tears, and turning into a monster to enact incredible violence. You have no immortal existence to safeguard for centuries or longer, nor time to bide; you have to get your business done now, in a human lifespan or less, because while Garou might theoretically live to over a century, they usually don't ever break a few decades after their First Change. While vampires typically have dulled emotions, for Garou, they get turned up to 11. Or 12.<br /> <br /> It's also about being born the way you were, for better or worse, and being set apart from communities that aren't your own. And even when you might find some kind of deeper acceptance with other Garou, the first tenet of the litany* is there to make it weird. You might even have been born as a wolf, or one of the rare survivors of the affection that happens when the first tenet gets broken (in the Dark Ages, breaking it is dealt with way more harshly than in modern times, typically with the parents and child or children getting exiled at the absolute most merciful; more often, they're executing and the Crinos-born kid gets torn to pieces.)<br /> <br /> While Kindred existence revolves around being around humans to hunt, Garou tend to be far away from any population center in the Dark Ages, with only the oddball Warders of Men (future Tetrasomians/Iron Riders/Glass Walkers) living around villages and castles. They safeguard their base of operations as a sacred territory (which it usually is in a very literal sense) and tend to the matters of wild spirits while hunting down and killing horrid monsters.<br /> <br /> In the course of doing so, they will experience permanent wounds. Another vastly different hallmark of W:tA compared to V:tM, battle scars are the end result of taking egregious damage, often what would have otherwise killed the character. They bring with them tales of Glory, though it's generally more sustainable to let a Galliard learn and tell your stories than having the battles' outcomes written on a body that ends up breaking down way sooner than it would otherwise. This is, again, in stark contrast to Vampire, where confrontations are to be avoided and anyone who engages in them preferentially will be a loose cannon by Kindred standards.<br /> <br /> That's because instead of immortal elders, Garou are in touch with the spirits of their ancestors. They can be summoned through cultural practices, but some Garou simply have a deep connection that allows them to host the spirits, briefly and with effort, in order to guide the descendant and bolster their efforts. Being a part of Garou culture involves singing the praises of said ancestor-spirits, even though they often weren't the most admirable people in life. In fact, having to step around the dignity of their forebears if they want to get anything done tends to be a major reason why the world goes to shit over the next few centuries; the Garou were hemmed in by needing to avoid reconciling with the Fera or acknowledging failings in their attention to the Wyrm and Weaver, and you can already see the outcome of that, though it could be great fun to play a W:tDA game where you turn things around centuries earlier.<br /> <br /> Also, on that note, the rails that drive the Vampire metaplot are not really present in Werewolf. PC packs tend to be much more important than the PC coteries that get swept aside and forced to merely watch events transpire because a writer had a mandate to kill Baba Yaga or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}